  "body": "Fixes #6578, which identified a gap where _indeterminateness_ could not be specified statically, blocking static HTML generators and server-side rendering processes from being able to use indeterminate checkboxes without resorting to invoking JavaScript. To fill this gap, I'm adding a `defaultindeterminate` content attribute that is reflected by a `defaultIndeterminate` IDL attribute (not the existing `indeterminate` IDL attribute). A _dirty indeterminateness_ concept is added, and parallels the existing concept of _dirty checkedness_, to allow interaction and usage of the `indeterminate` IDL attribute to separate the control from the \"default\" value.\n\nThe name choice is in line with other groups' recent decisions, such as Open UI choosing `initiallyopen` over a live `open` content attribute (see https://github.com/openui/open-ui/issues/311#issuecomment-1050192589). It also helps address confusion around the (lack of) liveness between the content attribute and the actual value of the control.\n\nAdditionally, introducing a new _dirty indeterminateness_ concept instead of overloading _dirty checkedness_ better matches existing user agent behavior, where the `indeterminate` IDL property doesn't establish _dirty checkedness_. User interaction would establish _dirty indeterminateness_, in addition to _dirty checkedness_.\n\nExplainer: https://github.com/MicrosoftEdge/MSEdgeExplainers/blob/main/DefaultIndeterminate/explainer.md\n\n-----\n\n- [ ] At least two implementers are interested (and none opposed):\n   * Chromium\n   * …\n- [ ] [Tests](https://github.com/web-platform-tests/wpt) are written and can be reviewed and commented upon at:\n   * … <!-- If these tests are tentative, link a PR to make them non-tentative. -->\n- [ ] [Implementation bugs](https://github.com/whatwg/meta/blob/main/MAINTAINERS.md#handling-pull-requests) are filed:\n   * Chromium: …\n   * Gecko: …\n   * WebKit: …\n   * Deno (only for timers, structured clone, base64 utils, channel messaging, module resolution, web workers, and web storage): …\n   * Node.js (only for timers, structured clone, base64 utils, channel messaging, and module resolution): …\n- [ ] Corresponding [HTML AAM](https://w3c.github.io/html-aam/) & [ARIA in HTML](https://w3c.github.io/html-aria/) issues & PRs:\n- [ ] [MDN issue](https://github.com/whatwg/meta/blob/main/MAINTAINERS.md#handling-pull-requests) is filed: …\n- [ ] The top of this comment includes a [clear commit message](https://github.com/whatwg/meta/blob/main/COMMITTING.md) to use. <!-- If you created this PR from a single commit, Github copied its message. Otherwise, you need to add a commit message yourself. -->\n\n(See [WHATWG Working Mode: Changes](https://whatwg.org/working-mode#changes) for more details.)\n\n\n<!--\n    This comment and the below content is programmatically generated.\n    You may add a comma-separated list of anchors you'd like a\n    direct link to below (e.g. #idl-serializers, #idl-sequence):\n\n    Don't remove this comment or modify anything below this line.\n    If you don't want a preview generated for this pull request,\n    just replace the whole of this comment's content by \"no preview\"\n    and remove what's below.\n-->\n***\n<a href=\"https://whatpr.org/html/13224/acknowledgements.html\" title=\"Last updated on Nov 23, 2026, 9:12 PM UTC (d48b03b)\">/acknowledgements.html</a>  ( <a href=\"https://whatpr.org/html/13224/546d834...d48b03b/acknowledgements.html\" title=\"Last updated on Nov 23, 2026, 9:12 PM UTC (d48b03b)\">diff</a> )\n<a href=\"https://whatpr.org/html/13224/indices.html\" title=\"Last updated on Nov 23, 2026, 9:12 PM UTC (d48b03b)\">/indices.html</a>  ( <a href=\"https://whatpr.org/html/13224/546d834...d48b03b/indices.html\" title=\"Last updated on Nov 23, 2026, 9:12 PM UTC (d48b03b)\">diff</a> )\n<a href=\"https://whatpr.org/html/13224/input.html\" title=\"Last updated on Nov 23, 2026, 9:12 PM UTC (d48b03b)\">/input.html</a>  ( <a href=\"https://whatpr.org/html/